Cuesta College


**Salary:** $66,696.00 - $81,072.00 Annually

**Job Type:** Full Time - 12 Months/ 100% FTE

**Job Number:** FY2627-00084

**Location:** Various Off-Campus Locations, CA

**Department:** Instruction

**Closing:** 12/3/2026 11:59 PM Pacific


Job Description Summary


DEFINITION


Under the general supervision of the Aviation Program Director and in collaboration with program faculty and the Dean of Skilled Trades & Technology/Health & Wellness, provide technical assistance, shop maintenance, department airplane repair, and equipment maintenance in support of the Aviation program, and perform other related duties as required within the program.


DISTINGUISHING CHARACTERISTICS


This position is distinguished from other Laboratory Technician classes in that incumbents must be knowledgeable in aviation areas and the use of aviation-related equipment, and be able to maintain related equipment and materials.


Incumbents in this position promote student learning outcomes and Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) support by ensuring that instructional labs are well-maintained and equipped with tools and equipment that assist the students.


ABOUT THE COLLEGE


Where You Will Work


Serving all of San Luis Obispo County, Cuesta College has provided comprehensive associate degree offerings, certificates, and community programs to the region since 1964. The main campus is located along scenic Highway 1, west of San Luis Obispo and east of the beaches of the Pacific Ocean. Cuesta College has a North County Campus in Paso Robles, and South County Center, in Arroyo Grande.


Who We Are


Equity, diversity, and inclusion are essential to our culture and the work we do. Cuesta College is proud to be a designated Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) committed to racial and socio-economic diversity as it reflects our communities and student populations. We actively seek to attract candidates who share this commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion. As part of the Cuesta College team, you can expect to be part of a collaborative community of faculty, classified professionals, administrators, students, and community partners advancing educational excellence with intentional support services leading to student success and completion.


Additional information about the college can be found at https://www.cuesta.edu/about/index.html

The college planning documents can be found at https://www.cuesta.edu/about/collegeplans/index.html

Our Student Equity Action Plan can be found at https://www.cuesta.edu/about/info/student-equity-initiatives/equity/index.html

We offer comprehensive benefit options. Information about benefits can be found at https://www.cuesta.edu/about/human-resources/benefits/index.html


Essential Functions & Qualifications


ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS


Ensure repaired or tested parts meet strict safety and regulatory standards;

Diagnose and repair malfunctioning parts or systems at a component level;

Disassemble, clean, inspect, repair, and reassemble parts according to specifications;

Conduct quality checks and assist in process improvements;

Calibrate tools and test equipment to ensure accuracy;

Maintain accurate records of inspections, tests, maintenance actions, and parts usage;

Interpret and follow technical manuals, schematics, and blueprints;

Perform aviation lab/simulation shop maintenance, support, and repairs;

Assist with the development of the department budget, as required;

Maintain equipment logs;

Order and maintain adequate instructional supplies for the department and maintain inventories as necessary to support student success;

Inspect Aviation labs to be consistent with student activities and supervise installation of new and old equipment;

Estimate the scope and cost of work assignments and select and order necessary tools and materials to complete job(s) while keeping within budget;

Maintain and verify safe operation of department hand and power tools; ensure laboratories, supply rooms, lecture/demonstration areas, and any special purpose areas are maintained in an orderly and neat manner;

Design, construct, assemble, adjust, test, and clean equipment and apparatus used in laboratory settings, demonstrations, and special projects;

Repair and calibrate complex instruments and equipment;

Maintain HazMat documentation and storage practices;

Inspect, identify, and report unsafe facilities or equipment following FAA regulations;

Assist in overall hangar cleanup and maintain a neat and orderly lab facility with the instructor;

Operate hoists and other equipment; and

Perform other related duties as required.


QUALIFICATIONS


**Education:**  
Required


Equivalent to graduation from the twelfth grade; and

Completion of the FAA Airman Certification Standards for the General aviation maintenance subjects or equivalent.


Preferred


Associate degree, from an accredited institution in related trades or technical area;

Completion of the FAA Airman Certification Standards for Airframe and Powerplant.


**Experience:**  
Required


Demonstrated understanding of aircraft systems and technical drawings; and

Demonstrated knowledge with aviation maintenance regulations (FAA, EASA, or military standards).


**Knowledge of:**  
Aviation repair;

Material Safety Data Sheets;

Safe working practices;

Tools, materials, methods, and terminology used in Aviation areas;

Methods and practices used in the maintenance of tools, machinery, and equipment;

Safe working practices;

Hazardous Communications Regulations - "Right to Know";

Fire Prevention, codes, and extinguishers;

CPR and First Aid;

Current technologies, personal computer, and associated office software such as word processing, spreadsheet, presentation, and/or database software;

